# These scripts are authored on Windows and executed on Linux -- as hooks in
# cloud sessions and as CI steps. Git's autocrlf would check them out with CRLF
# line endings, and bash on Linux then fails on the trailing carriage return
# with errors that point at the wrong thing entirely ("bad interpreter: no such
# file or directory" on a file that is plainly there).
#
# Forcing LF is what makes one copy of a script work on both.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
